== Theorems <sec-theorems>


#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[*Theorem 1.* #emph[=== Fermat’s Last Theorem <fermats-last-theorem>
For , there are no positive integers , ,  such that .

]] <thm-fermat>

#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[_Proof._ The proof was completed by Andrew Wiles in 1995 and is too long to include here.

 #h(1fr) □]

#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[*Definition 1.* === Group <group>
A group is a set  with a binary operation satisfying closure, associativity, identity, and invertibility.

] <def-group>

#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[*Lemma 1.* #emph[Every finite group has an element of order dividing the group order.

]] <lem-helper>

#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[*Corollary 1.* #emph[Every group of prime order is cyclic.

]] <cor-consequence>

#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[*Example 1.* The integers under addition form a group.

] <exm-integers>

#block(width: 100%, above: 1em, below: 1em)[*Remark 1.* Groups are fundamental to abstract algebra.

] <rem-note>

By \Theorem 1 and \Definition 1, we see the connection. Also see \Lemma 1, \Corollary 1, \Example 1, and \Remark 1.

